{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_macros.html.j2" as m with context %}
{% block title %}Capsid Hub — reproducible containers for bioinformatics{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section class="opening">
  <div class="opening-text">
    <p class="kicker sc">A registry of reproducible containers for bioinformatics</p>
    <h1>Container images whose contents can be stated, checked and rebuilt.</h1>
    <p class="abstract"><span class="sc">Abstract.</span>
      Capsid builds each bioinformatics tool into an OCI image from a declarative recipe and a lockfile
      that names every dependency by checksum. Images are built for x86-64 and, where the tool supports it, ARM64; they are tested, signed and
      attested in public continuous integration, then pulled and tested again on native hardware of each
      architecture. This hub holds the recipes and documents, image by image, what was installed, how it
      was built and how to verify it.</p>
    <p class="entry">
      <a href="catalogue/index.html" class="lead-link">Browse the catalogue</a>
      <span class="sep">or</span>
      <a href="method/index.html">read the method</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <figure class="fig-capsid" id="fig1">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 240 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="fig1-cap" data-capsid>
      <circle cx="120" cy="120" r="34" class="genome"/>
      <path d="M100 120 q10 -16 20 0 t20 0" class="genome-strand"/>
      {% for l in capsid_lines %}
      <line x1="{{ l.x1 }}" y1="{{ l.y1 }}" x2="{{ l.x2 }}" y2="{{ l.y2 }}" class="{{ 'back' if l.back else 'front' }}"/>
      {% endfor %}
    </svg>
    <figcaption id="fig1-cap"><span class="figno">Fig. 1.</span> The image as a capsid. A hardened shell
      (numeric non-root user, read-only tool tree, signature) encloses the payload: one tool and its locked
      dependency closure. Icosahedron, 20 faces, 12 vertices. <span class="hint">Drag to rotate.</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="numbered" id="inventory">
  <h2><span class="secno">1</span>Inventory</h2>
  <div class="body">
    <table class="booktabs inventory">
      <caption><span class="figno">Table 1.</span> Contents of this hub at compilation ({{ build_date }}).</caption>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tools</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.tools }}</td><td class="note">distinct programs with at least one published version</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Images</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.images }}</td><td class="note">{{ inventory.tool_images }} tool versions and {{ inventory.stacks }} multi-tool stacks</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Multi-architecture</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.multiarch }}</td><td class="note">images published for both linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 under one tag</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Locked artefacts</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.artefacts }}</td><td class="note">distinct packages named by URL and SHA-256 across all lockfiles</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Locked payload</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.bytes | bytes }}</td><td class="note">compressed size of the locked Conda packages (PyPI lockfiles record no sizes)</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Package ecosystems</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.conda }} / {{ inventory.pypi }}</td><td class="note">images with Conda (pixi) / PyPI (uv) packages; a stack can have both</td></tr>
        {% if digests_resolved %}
        <tr><th scope="row">Digests resolved</th><td class="num">{{ inventory.digests }} / {{ inventory.images }}</td><td class="note">images found in the registry at compilation, referenced by digest below</td></tr>
        {% endif %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="numbered" id="premises">
  <h2><span class="secno">2</span>Premises</h2>
  <div class="body">
    <p>A tag such as <code>samtools:1.25</code> names a program, not an environment. The numbers a pipeline
      produces also depend on the exact builds of compression libraries, the C runtime and dozens of other
      packages, which differ between two builds of the same tag made a month apart. Capsid treats that
      environment as an object to be published alongside the image:</p>
    <ol class="propositions">
      <li><strong>The closure is locked.</strong> Every image is installed from a lockfile that lists each
        package by URL and SHA-256, per architecture. The lockfile is in the repository, inside the image, and
        reproduced on each image page of this site.</li>
      <li><strong>The build is attested.</strong> Images are built by a public workflow from a pinned base image
        and a dated Debian snapshot, then signed with a short-lived certificate bound to that workflow. An SPDX
        SBOM and SLSA provenance travel with the image.</li>
      <li><strong>The result is checked where it runs.</strong> After publication, the signed digest is pulled on
        native amd64 and arm64 machines and the recipe's acceptance test is run again.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="numbered" id="method">
  <h2><span class="secno">3</span>From recipe to verified image</h2>
  <div class="body">
    <figure class="schematic" id="fig2">
      <ol class="stages">
        <li><span class="stage-no">i</span><strong>Recipe</strong><span class="io">recipe.yaml</span><span class="what">tool, version, packages, test</span></li>
        <li><span class="stage-no">ii</span><strong>Lock</strong><span class="io">pixi.lock · requirements.lock</span><span class="what">closure solved once, by checksum</span></li>
        <li><span class="stage-no">iii</span><strong>Build</strong><span class="io">amd64 ∥ arm64</span><span class="what">base by digest, apt by snapshot</span></li>
        <li><span class="stage-no">iv</span><strong>Test</strong><span class="io">capsid test</span><span class="what">acceptance command, exit code</span></li>
        <li><span class="stage-no">v</span><strong>Sign · attest</strong><span class="io">Cosign · SPDX · SLSA</span><span class="what">keyless, logged in Rekor</span></li>
        <li><span class="stage-no">vi</span><strong>Verify</strong><span class="io">native runners</span><span class="what">pull digest, test again</span></li>
      </ol>
      <figcaption><span class="figno">Fig. 2.</span> Publication pipeline. Stages i–ii happen in a pull request and
        are reviewed by a maintainer; iii–vi run in <code>publish-release</code> after the merge, the only job holding
        write access to the registry. Details in <a href="method/index.html">Method</a>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="numbered" id="catalogue">
  <h2><span class="secno">4</span>Catalogue</h2>
  <div class="body">
    <table class="booktabs tools">
      <caption><span class="figno">Table 2.</span> Tools in the hub, with the build of their latest version.
        <em>Closure</em> counts the locked artefacts in one architecture of the image.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Versions</th><th>Build</th><th>Arch.</th><th class="num">Closure</th><th>Licence</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
{{ m.tool_rows(tools[:6], root) }}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="more"><a href="catalogue/index.html">All {{ tools | length }} tools, searchable and filterable →</a>
      {% if stacks %}<span class="sep">·</span><a href="stacks/index.html">{{ stacks | length }} stacks →</a>{% endif %}</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% if example %}
<section class="numbered" id="example">
  <h2><span class="secno">5</span>A worked example</h2>
  <div class="body">
    <p>Running <a href="{{ example.url }}">{{ example.name }} {{ example.version }}</a> in each supported environment.
      {% if example.digest %}The reference is pinned by digest, so it cannot be re-pointed by a later republish.
      {% else %}For published work, pin the image by digest (<code>…@sha256:…</code>); each image page lists it.{% endif %}</p>
    {{ m.usage(example, "ex") }}
    <p>More environments, HPC and offline clusters: <a href="guide/using/index.html">Using the images →</a></p>
    <p>Before relying on an image, verify that it was produced by this hub's publish workflow:</p>
    {{ m.verify(example) }}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="numbered" id="contribute">
  <h2><span class="secno">6</span>Contributing a tool</h2>
  <div class="body two-col">
    <div>
      <h3>By pull request</h3>
      <p>Add <code>recipes/&lt;tool&gt;/&lt;version&gt;/recipe.yaml</code>, run <code>capsid lock</code> to produce the
        lockfile and open a pull request. The audit workflow validates the schema, lints the recipe and builds and
        tests it without write permissions.</p>
      <p><a href="guide/contributing/index.html">Step-by-step guide →</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>By issue form</h3>
      <p>Fill in the <a href="{{ HUB_URL }}/issues/new/choose">New recipe</a> form. The recipe is built and tested in
        isolation; if it passes, a pull request is opened for review.</p>
      <h3>Upstream robot</h3>
      <p>Every Friday the hub checks Bioconda for tools released in the previous week and proposes recipes in a
        pull request. Nothing is published before a maintainer merges it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
